{
  "id": "2026-10-07-enhanced-geothermal",
  "title": "The first enhanced geothermal power plant is now feeding the grid",
  "topic": "테크",
  "level": 2,
  "voice": "en-US-AndrewMultilingualNeural",
  "sentences": [
    "Good morning!",
    "Today's story is about a power plant that pulls energy from deep underground.",
    "A company called Fervo Energy has just switched on the world's first commercial enhanced geothermal plant, in Utah.",
    "Traditional geothermal only works in rare places where hot water sits close to the surface.",
    "Enhanced geothermal drills much deeper, down to rock that is hot almost everywhere.",
    "The idea borrows a lot from the oil and gas industry.",
    "Engineers pump water down through the hot rock, and it comes back up hot enough to spin turbines.",
    "Unlike solar and wind, it can run around the clock, no matter the weather.",
    "The first section produces about thirty-three megawatts.",
    "The whole site could eventually reach four gigawatts, enough for millions of homes.",
    "It went from breaking ground to the grid in just twenty-three months, ahead of schedule.",
    "Google and a big California utility have already signed up to buy the power.",
    "Fervo also raised nearly two billion dollars when it went public in May.",
    "The big question now is whether costs can come down fast enough to compete.",
    "If you care about clean, steady power, keep an eye on this one. Have a great day!"
  ],
  "summary_ko": [
    "미국 Fervo Energy 가 유타주에 세계 첫 상업용 '강화 지열(EGS)' 발전소를 가동했다. 깊이 뚫어 뜨거운 암반에 물을 넣고 증기로 터빈을 돌린다.",
    "태양광·풍력과 달리 24시간 돈다. 1단계 33MW, 부지 전체로는 최대 4GW 까지 가능하고, 착공부터 계통 연결까지 23개월로 예정보다 빨랐다.",
    "구글과 캘리포니아 전력회사가 이미 전력 구매를 약속했고, 회사는 5월 상장으로 19억 달러를 모았다. 남은 숙제는 단가다."
  ],
